# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# python-barcode.md shows how this ledger applies them. Supported versions:
# Python 3.9 and later (pyproject.toml requires-python ">=3.9"); Pillow is
# optional (extra "images", unpinned), and both sides of the optional import
# at writer.py:33-42 run.
# Receivers: Barcode cannot be instantiated (its __init__ raises
# NotImplementedError, base.py:37-38), so it is no receiver of its own
# methods (judgement J1); every package barcode class overrides build and
# get_fullcode. BaseWriter is a plain public class whose __init__ takes the
# four callbacks, documented for subclassing (docs/writers.rst), so it is a
# receiver of its own methods (J3). A writer's callbacks are the bound
# methods that SVGWriter.__init__ and ImageWriter.__init__ pass, or client
# callables (opaque); register_callback types its callback as a bare
# Callable (B2: no package value).
default reject barcode.base.Barcode.__repr__, barcode.codabar.CODABAR.__str__, barcode.codex.Code128.__str__, barcode.codex.Code39.__str__, barcode.ean.EuropeanArticleNumber13.__str__, barcode.errors.BarcodeError.__str__, barcode.isxn.InternationalStandardBookNumber10.__str__, barcode.isxn.InternationalStandardSerialNumber.__str__, barcode.itf.ITF.__str__, barcode.upc.UniversalProductCodeA.__str__: no barcode object and no BarcodeError is formatted, printed, converted by str() or repr(), or used with % at this site; the values in the f-strings, str.format fields and print calls are str, int and float values (codes, digits, checksums, file names, colours, sizes, the version string, argparse strings), and every % in the package is an integer modulo

